          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            To work out how much paint a ceiling needs, multiply its area by the number of coats and divide by the low end of the label's coverage. Reduce coverage for texture, prime porous surfaces, plan for two coats and round up with a margin.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Smooth ceilings in average rooms usually need one to two gallons; textured and popcorn ceilings need much more. Our <a href="/best-ceiling-paint/">ceiling paint picks</a> compare hide and coverage across the best options.
          </p>
